From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:06:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: iomfb_m4: send external flips with their
 own completion by default

A T8132 external output scans a DRM framebuffer out directly where it
can (t8132_ext_present() tries that first on every T8132 board, the
J604's HDMI and Type-C outputs included). With t8132_ext_swap_depth at
2, the default so far, a frame's flip event goes out once its swap is
accepted (A407) while the previous frame is still on screen until the
swap's own completion (D590), as the parameter's text says.

DRM hands the previous framebuffer back to the compositor with the flip
event. A compositor that renders on the flip event into a round-robin
swapchain of two buffers (Aquamarine's rotates, age = length) then draws
its next frame into the buffer being scanned out, for as long as the
panel takes to reach the swap's tick.

Default the depth to 1, so that every external flip event comes with
its swap's D590 and the previous buffer is off screen when it is handed
back. The parameter stays, with 2 as an opt-in for measurements.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c | 13 +++++++------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index d9d36d0c63..fb649a9ef8 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -150,13 +150,14 @@ struct iomfb_m4_ext_mode {
 
 /*
  * How many external direct swaps may be in flight (A407 answered, the D590
- * not yet in), 1 or 2, read at each frame. At depth 1 every flip event is
- * sent with its swap's D590. At depth 2 a frame's flip event can be sent
- * before the firmware confirms that the frame replaced the previous one, so a
- * compositor may draw into a buffer that is still on screen.
+ * not yet in), 1 (default) or 2, read at each frame. At depth 1 every flip
+ * event is sent with its swap's D590. At depth 2 a frame's flip event can be
+ * sent before the firmware confirms that the frame replaced the previous one,
+ * so a compositor may draw into a buffer that is still on screen: one with a
+ * two-buffer swapchain draws its next frame into exactly that buffer.
  */
 #define DCP_M4_EXT_INFLIGHT	2
-static unsigned int t8132_ext_swap_depth = DCP_M4_EXT_INFLIGHT;
+static unsigned int t8132_ext_swap_depth = 1;
 
 static int t8132_ext_swap_depth_set(const char *val, const struct kernel_param *kp)
 {
@@ -170,7 +171,7 @@ static const struct kernel_param_ops t8132_ext_swap_depth_ops = {
 
 module_param_cb(t8132_ext_swap_depth, &t8132_ext_swap_depth_ops, &t8132_ext_swap_depth, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(t8132_ext_swap_depth,
-		 "J713 external direct swaps in flight at most, 2 (default) or 1, from the next frame. At 2 a flip event can come before the firmware confirms the frame replaced the previous one, so a compositor may draw into a buffer still on screen; at 1 every flip event comes with its swap's completion");
+		 "T8132 external direct swaps in flight at most, 1 (default) or 2, from the next frame. At 1 every flip event comes with its swap's completion; at 2 a flip event can come before the firmware confirms the frame replaced the previous one, so a compositor may draw into a buffer still on screen");
 static bool swap_timestamps = true;
 module_param(swap_timestamps, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(swap_timestamps,
-- 
